                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b99d7d45-5df1-3d66-98b7-dfbd85ed65c1",
                        "entry_id": "d08ecd3e-bfb2-38fb-9b1d-07a8ed82ff96",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To seize power from another, usually by illegitimate means."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3bb0a72c-3daf-4c59-bc8a-e0dc5546be62",
                                "sense_id": "b99d7d45-5df1-3d66-98b7-dfbd85ed65c1",
                                "text": "[S]o he dies,\nBut soon revives, Death over him no power\nShall long usurp […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "59a8516c-4ecf-4325-a4ce-24ae3e885efb",
                                "sense_id": "b99d7d45-5df1-3d66-98b7-dfbd85ed65c1",
                                "text": "Most Republicans in Congress are complying as Mr. Trump usurps the power of the national legislature, as laid out in Article 1 of the Constitution."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3f15d085-b892-3b01-acff-1422d7d95c5a",
                        "entry_id": "d08ecd3e-bfb2-38fb-9b1d-07a8ed82ff96",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To use and assume the coat of arms of another person."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8abb402b-396f-3148-9a3b-27c833ac18cd",
                        "entry_id": "d08ecd3e-bfb2-38fb-9b1d-07a8ed82ff96",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To take the place rightfully belonging to someone or something else."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "af512158-a5ca-407a-b056-1cee726335ef",
                                "sense_id": "8abb402b-396f-3148-9a3b-27c833ac18cd",
                                "text": "But if now / You ſhould (as cruell fathers do) proclame / Your right, and Tyrant like uſurp the glory / Of my peculiar honours, not deriv'd / From ſucceſſary, but purchas'd with my bloud, / Then I muſt ſtand firſt Champion for my ſelfe, / Againſt all interpoſers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "88ffbdac-593c-40f9-8b39-3d6e1ad71ccb",
                                "sense_id": "8abb402b-396f-3148-9a3b-27c833ac18cd",
                                "text": "Jones answered all his questions with much civility, though he never remembered to have seen the petty-fogger before; and though he concluded, from the outward appearance and behaviour of the man, that he usurped a freedom with his betters, to which he was by no means intitled."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fbc60ba5-147b-303e-8624-f3ba017efed1",
                        "entry_id": "d08ecd3e-bfb2-38fb-9b1d-07a8ed82ff96",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To make use of."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b1335200-4ea4-4c11-b76a-30f4163f07c8",
                                "sense_id": "fbc60ba5-147b-303e-8624-f3ba017efed1",
                                "text": "\"[…] especially considering that even Matter it self, in which they tumble and wallow, which they feel with their hands and usurp with all their Senses […]\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
